[1mx0ne Engine cloud session <SESSION>[0m: deleted (ended)
  provider  gcp, project x0ne-test-project, zone us-central1-a
  VM        x0ne-engine-<SESSION> (a3-highgpu-1g spot, Intel TDX + 1x H100)
  model     qwen3:0.6b
  verdict   [1;32mVERIFIED[0m (by the relay, on this machine)
  cost      [33m# USD so far (estimate, 6.51 USD/h); at most 5.97 USD[0m
  note      estimated cost # USD

[1mNot protected:[0m
- this machine: malware in your session can read the local key and your questions;
- Google's firmware: the binary Google signed is fetched and measured, its source is not published; RTMR0 (the host's TD HOB, Secure Boot variables, ACPI tables and boot variables) is pinned to the reference's events as one boot showed them, not audited;
- revocation: the TD's PCK is checked against Intel's PCK CRL, its PCK CA and Intel's TCB signing certificate against Intel's root CA CRL, both fetched live; the OCSP responses a document staples about NVIDIA's signing chain are judged under the policy the verdict names, a verified revoked refused either way; no TD staples them yet;
- the platform's patch level: under the default transparent TCB policy the host is accepted on Intel's standard TCB collateral, and what Intel's latest collateral rates not fixed is named on the VERIFIED line and in each receipt, not refused; `--tcb-policy strict` refuses it;
- the GPU verdict comes from NVIDIA's NRAS service; each connection's GPU evidence answers a nonce derived from that connection's TLS exporter and TDX quote, but CPU and GPU are bound by the TD's software, not by the hardware (Hopper): the link falls with the CPU TEE (TEE.fail);
- physical attacks on memory (TEE.fail, DDR5 interposer, 2025-10) and side channels;
- a compromise of Intel's, NVIDIA's or Google's roots;
- availability: Google can stop the VM (spot); it sees times, sizes, IP addresses and the bill;
- the image reference: the relay takes one only with a signature by the x0ne archive key pinned in its build, and a relay built before the signing ceremony pins none and refuses them all; whoever holds the signing subkey can sign any image, and a revocation reaches you only with a new release;
- the behaviour of the model itself.

[1mReported by the relay for this session:[0m
- fake relay: nothing was verified
[exit 0]

